You'll need the following to delete the `tmpDir` itself.
```suggestion

                @Override
                public FileVisitResult postVisitDirectory(Path dir, IOException exc) throws IOException {
                    Files.delete(dir);
                    return FileVisitResult.CONTINUE;
                }
```

I think you'll now have to do a null check before the walk.
```suggestion
        public void close() throws IOException {
            if (tmpDir == null) {
                return;
            }
```

Alternatively, you could move the creation of `tmpDir` to the `CgroupMountInfoStub` constructor because then in case of an error the `close` method will not be called.
